  "notes": "{語|かた}らう is an intransitive godan verb that conveys a warm, leisurely quality of conversation. It is more literary and poetic than {話|はな}す or しゃべる.\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{語|かた}らっている indicates an ongoing conversation.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- Xと{語|かた}らう (converse with X)\n- Xについて{語|かた}らう (talk about X)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {友|とも}と{語|かた}らう (talk with friends)\n- {夢|ゆめ}を{語|かた}らう (share one's dreams)\n- {酒|さけ}を{飲|の}みながら{語|かた}らう (talk over drinks)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {語|かた}らう vs {話|はな}す: {語|かた}らう implies unhurried, heartfelt conversation, while {話|はな}す is a neutral, general word for speaking or talking.\n- {語|かた}らう vs {語|かた}る: {語|かた}る means to narrate or tell a story (often one-directional), while {語|かた}らう implies mutual, back-and-forth exchange.",
